KIRP Enterprise — Short Working Rules for Cursor
(Concise, strict, and safe)
1. Architecture Rules (Do Not Break)
Keep the structure exactly as:
core/ engines, agents/ handlers, api/ routers, workers/ background tasks, ui/ dashboard.
No new top‑level folders.
No changes to docker-compose.yml or .env unless explicitly requested.
2. Event‑Sourcing & Multi‑Tenancy
No direct DB mutations. All changes must be events.
Always propagate tenant_id, space_id, user_id.
All external actions must go through Governance.
3. RAG + Agents
RAG context must be passed consistently.
No direct LLM calls outside agents/.
All new agents must use AgentFramework.register().
4. Schema Engine
Until fully implemented:
No raw SQL.
No assumptions about schema persistence.
Use only the provided placeholders.
5. Legacy Integration
Use old KIRP code only as inspiration, not copy‑paste.
Modernize and integrate into the new architecture.
6. Allowed Work (Green Light)
Implement Schema Engine (models, migrations, queries).
Implement EventPipeline fully.
Improve RAG (no zero vectors, better API usage).
Upgrade agents and context handling.
Migrate legacy agents into AgentFramework.
7. Safety Checklist
Before any change, verify:
[ ] No imports or APIs were broken
[ ] Event‑sourcing preserved
[ ] Multi‑tenancy preserved
[ ] Governance enforced
[ ] No infra changes
[ ] No duplicate logic
[ ] Output validated (Pydantic preferred)